# Design <-> Token discrepancies

Use a dedicated section to track mismatches between Figma design intent and token usage.

## Section name and placement

- Section title: `## Discrepancias detectadas`
- Component docs: place after `## States` and before `## Usage Guidelines`.
- If no discrepancies exist, omit the section.

## Required table format

Use this exact table schema:

| Discrepancia | Impacto | Accion pendiente | Estado |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |

### Field guidance

- `Discrepancia`: factual mismatch (hardcoded value, missing token, naming mismatch, unmapped variant).
- `Impacto`: short impact statement on consistency/usability/maintenance.
- `Accion pendiente`: concrete remediation task.
- `Estado`: `open`, `accepted`, or `resolved`.

## Content rules

- Record only verifiable mismatches.
- Do not invent root causes.
- If evidence is incomplete, mark the row with `TBD` in the relevant cell.
